End the paragraph before a \code that follows its text directly.
\code skips the end of its own line, so with the paragraph still open the
code's first line ran into the paragraph and the block came out empty.
A \par at the end of the preceding line (line count preserved) closes the
paragraph first.  Sites: dict-flow.tex:413, dict-conses.tex:4199 and
:4203, dict-sequences.tex:103.
--- dict-flow.tex
+++ dict-flow.tex
@@ -413,1 +413,1 @@
-an access to the \term{function cell}, as in:
+an access to the \term{function cell}, as in:\par
--- dict-conses.tex
+++ dict-conses.tex
@@ -4199,1 +4199,1 @@
-The effect of
+The effect of\par
@@ -4203,1 +4203,1 @@
-is roughly equivalent to
+is roughly equivalent to\par
--- dict-sequences.tex
+++ dict-sequences.tex
@@ -103,1 +103,1 @@
-From a functional standpoint,
+From a functional standpoint,\par
